{"name":"Eyeshadow Viola","hex":"#ada6c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eyeshadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of eye shadow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eyeshadow"},{"term":"viola","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowering plants, of the genus Viola, including the violets and pansies."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bowed  tenor instrument larger than a violin but smaller than a cello, used in orchestras and string quartets.","An organ stop with a similar tone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/viola"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eye shadow","blocks":[{"text":"Eye shadow is a cosmetic applied primarily to the eyelids to attract attention to the wearer's eyes, making them stand out or look more attractive. Eye shadow can also be applied under the eyes, on the cheeks, or to brow bones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Colours_-_make_up.jpg/330px-Colours_-_make_up.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye_shadow"},{"title":"Viola","blocks":[{"text":"The viola ( vee-OH-lə, Italian: [ˈvjɔːla, viˈɔːla]) is a string instrument of the violin family, and is usually bowed when played. The viola is slightly larger than the violin and has a lower sound. Since the 18th century, it has been the middle or alto voice of the violin family, between the violin (which is tuned a perfect fifth higher) and the cello (which is tuned an octave lower). The strings from low to high are typically tuned to C3, G3, D4, and A4."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Bratsche.jpg/330px-Bratsche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viola"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Duochrome_super_macro_eye_shadow_by_m.a.c.%